<title>FRANCE: Algerian sea company makes $7.46 million profit.</title>
<headline>Algerian sea company makes $7.46 million profit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's National Maritime Passenger Transport Company made a net profit of 418 million dinars ($7.46 million) in 1995, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Sunday.</p>
<p>It gave no comparative figures but said the profit was realised on a turnover of 7.02 billion dinars.</p>
<p>APS added that 6.17 million dinars would be distributed to workers and 398 million dinars to meet previous deficits of the company whose capital was 15 million dinars.</p>
<p>($1 = 56 dinars)</p>
</text>
